# Example rules

These are common starting points, written out so you can build them in the
rule editor. Each one says what it is for and what to watch out for.

<Callout type="info" title="Starting points, not recommendations">

  The numbers here are examples of how people often set these rules up. They
  are not medical advice and they may not suit you. Agree your own thresholds
  with your diabetes care team, and keep your CGM and pump alarms switched on
  alongside Nocturne.

</Callout>

Values are given in mg/dL with mmol/L in brackets. "Rows" are the conditions in
the rule's **Condition** card, and "all of" or "any of" is the choice at the top
of it.

## Urgent low

| | |
|---|---|
| **Rows** | Glucose below 54 (3.0) |
| **Severity** | Critical |
| **For at least** | Off |

The alert that must always get through. Critical means Do Not Disturb never
holds it back. No "for at least" delay, because a late alert here costs more
than a false one.

## Low

| | |
|---|---|
| **Rows** | Glucose below 70 (3.9), for at least 15 min |
| **Severity** | Warning |

A gentler low alert that ignores a single odd reading, such as a compression
low from lying on the sensor. Pair it with the urgent low above, which catches
anything serious straight away. See
[Conditions that must last](/docs/alerts/sustained) for how the delay works.

## Falling towards a low

| | |
|---|---|
| **Top** | any of |
| **Rows** | Glucose below 70 (3.9); **or** a group, all of: Glucose below 100 (5.5) and Rate of change falling at least 2 (0.11) a minute |
| **Severity** | Warning |

Alerts on a low, and also earlier on a fast fall towards one, such as during
exercise. See the worked example in
[Combining conditions](/docs/alerts/combining#groups).

## Predicted low

| | |
|---|---|
| **Rows** | Predicted glucose ≤ 70 (3.9) within 30 min |
| **Severity** | Warning |

For loops that upload a forecast (AAPS, Trio). Warns before the low arrives.
Forecasts change every few minutes, so expect some alerts that never turn into
lows. On a setup with no forecast, this rule never fires, so keep an ordinary
low rule as well.

## High that does not go away

| | |
|---|---|
| **Rows** | Glucose above 250 (13.9), for at least 60 min |
| **Severity** | Warning |

Waits long enough that a normal rise after food is not flagged, and speaks up
when a high is lasting, which can be a sign of a blocked or failed infusion set.

## Quiet after dinner

| | |
|---|---|
| **Top** | all of |
| **Rows** | Glucose above 180 (10.0), for at least 30 min; **and** NOT Time of day 18:00 to 20:00 |

A high alert that stays quiet through the rise you expect after the evening
meal.

## Signal loss

| | |
|---|---|
| **Rows** | Signal loss: no reading for 30 min |
| **Severity** | Warning, or Critical overnight |

When readings stop, every glucose rule goes quiet with them. This is the rule
that tells you. Every setup that relies on alerts should have one.

## Loop has stopped

| | |
|---|---|
| **Rows** | Loop has stopped: more than 20 min |
| **Severity** | Warning |

For closed-loop users. A loop that stops has usually lost the pump or the CGM,
and the pump carries on with its own programmed settings. Add **Loop not enacting** as
well if your loop can run without being able to reach the pump.

## Pump left suspended

| | |
|---|---|
| **Rows** | Pump suspended: is, for at least 30 min |
| **Severity** | Warning |

Catches a pump suspended for a shower or a site change and not resumed.

## Tell someone else if nobody responds

| | |
|---|---|
| **Rows** | Other rule state: "Low" is unacknowledged, for at least 15 min |
| **Severity** | Critical |
| **Channels** | The second person's phone or chat |

Escalation. If the Low alert has been going for 15 minutes and nobody has
pressed **Acknowledge**, a second person is told. Acknowledging the Low alert
stops this one. Snoozing does not, because a snooze is not an acknowledgement.

Build the Low rule first, then pick it in this rule's **Other rule state** row.
If the Low rule is switched off or deleted, this rule stops being checked.

## Overnight only

| | |
|---|---|
| **Top** | all of |
| **Rows** | Glucose below 80 (4.4), for at least 10 min; **and** Time of day 22:00 to 07:00 |

A slightly higher low threshold at night only, when a low is less likely to be
noticed. The time window uses your time zone. As above, keep the "for at least"
row first.

## Site change reminder

| | |
|---|---|
| **Rows** | Site age ≥ 72 h |
| **Severity** | Info |

Info alerts are sent once and marked as acknowledged straight away, so a
reminder does not keep nagging. Use **Sensor age** in days for a sensor
reminder, or **Reservoir** ≤ 20 U for a refill reminder.

## Phone battery low

| | |
|---|---|
| **Rows** | Phone battery ≤ 20 % |
| **Severity** | Warning |

The phone that uploads readings running flat is one of the most common reasons
readings stop. A warning before it dies beats a signal loss alert after.
